From: MacBookPro16,1 hybrid graphics
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] PCI/thunderbolt/xhci: drive the MacBookPro16,1 Titan Ridge power sequence

On MacBookPro16,1 the JHL7540 Titan Ridge power sequence lives in ACPI, but
every firmware entry point is gated on !OSDW(): PEGn._INI only arms it when the
OS is not Darwin, and _WAK only calls ICMB() when that arming happened. Linux
answers _OSI("Darwin") on Apple hardware, so none of it runs. Across s2idle the
switch never comes back out of D3 -- eight devices in the two subtrees report
"Unable to change power state from D3hot to D0, device inaccessible", both xHCI
controllers report "Controller not ready at resume -19" and then "HC died", and
neither USB-C port works again until reboot.

macOS does not use _WAK for this either. AppleThunderboltNHIType3 drives the
same ACPI methods from the driver, which is why Apple gates them out for Darwin.
This implements that sequence, in its order:

  down   xHCI RTPC(0)                      xhci_pci_suspend()
         NHI Go2Sx over the VSEC mailbox, NHI RTPC(0)
                                           apple_tr_nhi_suspend_noirq()
         NHI0.SXFP(0), NHI0.XRST(1)        root-port suspend_late fixup
  up     NHI0.XRST(0), NHI0.TRPE(1, 0)     root-port resume_early fixup
         NHI RTPC(1)                       apple_tr_nhi_resume_noirq()
         xHCI RTPC(1)                      xhci_pci_resume()

Three things about it are not obvious and were each established by measurement:

Both RTPC votes are required. NHI RTPC writes PEGn.RTBT and xHCI RTPC writes
PEGn.RUSB; the upstream switch's POFF() is !RTBT && !RUSB, and RUSB defaults to
One. Without the xHCI half POFF() never becomes true and firmware keeps power.

SXFP(0) and XRST(1) must run from the root port's suspend_late fixup, not from
the NHI's suspend_noirq. SXFP(0) drives GPIO 0x03050007 low, which removes the
whole subtree from the bus; the PCI core still has to walk the NHI and the three
bridges above it into D3hot afterwards, and issuing it any earlier makes every
one of them fail. DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_SUSPEND_LATE on the root port runs at the
Fixup: label of pci_pm_suspend_noirq(), after this port's own D-state change and
after every device below it has suspended, which is the only safe moment.

The Go2Sx mailbox is answered by a firmware connection manager. Linux runs the
software CM on Apple hardware (icm.c refuses x86_apple_machine), and
tb_switch_suspend() has already set TB_LC_SX_CTRL_SLP on every link controller
over the control channel -- the same notification by another route, which is why
icl_nhi_suspend_noirq() skips this mailbox when !tb_switch_is_icm(). The command
is still sent because Apple sends it, but its timeout is expected and is logged
rather than treated as an error.

Also skip the host-router reset in tb_resume_noirq() when the platform firmware
did not participate in the sleep. It exists to undo topology the firmware may
have set up behind the driver's back, which cannot have happened during s2idle.

Verified on the reference machine: six pm_test=platform cycles and one real
123.7 s s2idle, all with zero Titan Ridge PM failures, TRPE(1,0) acquiring
PEGn.UPSB.AVND on the first attempt every time in 72 ms, and both controllers
subsequently reaching D3cold on their own when idle -- which the previous
pin-in-D0 bypass could never allow.

diff --git i/drivers/pci/quirks.c w/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index b09f27f7846f..796ea8e76cc3 100644
--- i/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ w/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/switchtec.h>
+#include <linux/mbp161-tb.h>
 #include "pci.h"
 
 static bool pcie_lbms_seen(struct pci_dev *dev, u16 lnksta)
@@ -3927,6 +3928,131 @@ static void quirk_apple_poweroff_thunderbolt(struct pci_dev *dev)
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_SUSPEND_LATE(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,
 			       PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_CACTUS_RIDGE_4C,
 			       quirk_apple_poweroff_thunderbolt);
+
+/*
+ * Apple: drive the Titan Ridge power sequence the way macOS does.
+ *
+ * On MacBookPro16,1 the JHL7540 power sequence lives in ACPI, but every
+ * firmware entry point is gated on !OSDW(): PEGn._INI only arms it when the OS
+ * is not Darwin, and _WAK only calls ICMB() when that arming happened.  Linux
+ * answers _OSI("Darwin") on Apple hardware, so none of it runs and the switch
+ * never comes back out of D3 -- the bridges report "Unable to change power
+ * state from D3hot to D0, device inaccessible" and the internal xHCI answers
+ * configuration cycles but not memory cycles.  macOS drives the same methods
+ * from its own driver rather than from _WAK, which is exactly why Apple gates
+ * them out for Darwin.  This is the Linux equivalent of that driver-side work.
+ *
+ * The sequence is AppleThunderboltNHIType3's, in its order:
+ *
+ *   down   xHCI RTPC(0)                    xhci_pci_suspend()
+ *          NHI Go2Sx over the VSEC mailbox, NHI RTPC(0)
+ *                                          apple_tr_nhi_suspend_noirq()
+ *          NHI0.SXFP(0), NHI0.XRST(1)      here, at suspend_late
+ *   up     NHI0.XRST(0), NHI0.TRPE(1, 0)   here, at resume_early
+ *          NHI RTPC(1)                     apple_tr_nhi_resume_noirq()
+ *          xHCI RTPC(1)                    xhci_pci_resume()
+ *
+ * The two RTPC votes are both load-bearing: NHI RTPC writes PEGn.RTBT, xHCI
+ * RTPC writes PEGn.RUSB, and the upstream switch's POFF() is
+ * !RTBT && !RUSB.  RUSB defaults to One, so without the xHCI half POFF()
+ * never becomes true and the firmware refuses to release power.
+ *
+ * SXFP(0) drives GPIO 0x03050007 low, which removes the controller from the
+ * bus, and TRPE(1) releases it and waits for PEGn.UPSB.AVND to answer, power
+ * cycling up to five times.  Because SXFP(0) takes the whole subtree away, it
+ * can only run once everything below the root port has already suspended --
+ * see the placement note on quirk_mbp161_type3_suspend().
+ *
+ * mbp161_tb_type3 is on by default and gated on DMI so it is inert elsewhere.
+ * To fall back to the old behaviour -- both controllers pinned in D0 across
+ * s2idle, which works but blocks any Thunderbolt power management -- boot with
+ *   mbp161_tb_type3=0 mbp161_tb_bypass=1
+ */
+static int mbp161_tb_type3 = 1;
+core_param(mbp161_tb_type3, mbp161_tb_type3, int, 0644);
+
+bool mbp161_tb_type3_wanted(void)
+{
+	return mbp161_tb_type3 && dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "MacBookPro16,1");
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mbp161_tb_type3_wanted);
+
+/*
+ * Type3 power-down on the PEG root port.  DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_SUSPEND_LATE runs
+ * at the Fixup: label of pci_pm_suspend_noirq(), which is the last statement
+ * of that function -- after this port's own D-state transition, and after every
+ * device below it has already suspended (children suspend before parents).
+ * That is the only safe moment to cut the rail.  Doing it from the NHI's
+ * suspend_noirq instead strands the NHI and the three bridges above it, which
+ * then all report "Unable to change power state from D0 to D3hot".
+ *
+ * SXFP(0) drives GPIO 0x03050007 low, which is the pin TRPE(1) releases on the
+ * way back, and leaves it in the driven-low state TRPE(1)'s guard requires.
+ * XRST(1) then arms XRTE and parks the link in L2 with the port in D3hot.
+ */
+static void quirk_mbp161_type3_suspend(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	acpi_handle port, nhi;
+
+	if (!mbp161_tb_type3_wanted())
+		return;
+	if (pci_pcie_type(dev) != PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
+		return;
+
+	port = ACPI_HANDLE(&dev->dev);
+	if (!port)
+		return;
+	if (ACPI_FAILURE(acpi_get_handle(port, "UPSB.DSB0.NHI0", &nhi)))
+		return;
+
+	pci_info(dev, "mbp161 type3: NHI0.SXFP(0) + NHI0.XRST(1)\n");
+	acpi_execute_simple_method(nhi, "SXFP", 0);
+	acpi_execute_simple_method(nhi, "XRST", 1);
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_SUSPEND_LATE(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x1905,
+			       quirk_mbp161_type3_suspend);
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_SUSPEND_LATE(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x1909,
+			       quirk_mbp161_type3_suspend);
+
+/*
+ * Type3 pre-PCI wake on the PEG root port.  PEG1/PEG2 have no _PS0 or _PS3 --
+ * only _PRT and _PRW -- so pci_pm_default_resume_early() touches nothing but
+ * the root port's own always-accessible config space, and PCEU() (which is
+ * what calls XRST(0) when XRTE is armed) belongs to the PEG scope and runs
+ * from DSB0._PS0, long after this.  That makes this hook the first thing to
+ * reach the Titan Ridge on the way back, and both calls below necessary:
+ * XRST(0) undoes the L2/D3hot park, TRPE(1,0) raises the rail SXFP(0) cut.
+ * Do not poll NHI PCI vendor ID from Linux: a config read of a still-dead
+ * Titan Ridge hard-freezes this machine.  TRPE(1) already waits for it.
+ */
+static void quirk_mbp161_type3_resume(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	union acpi_object args[2] = {
+		{ .integer = { ACPI_TYPE_INTEGER, 1 } },
+		{ .integer = { ACPI_TYPE_INTEGER, 0 } },
+	};
+	struct acpi_object_list list = { .count = 2, .pointer = args };
+	acpi_handle port, nhi;
+
+	if (!mbp161_tb_type3_wanted())
+		return;
+	if (pci_pcie_type(dev) != PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
+		return;
+
+	port = ACPI_HANDLE(&dev->dev);
+	if (!port)
+		return;
+	if (ACPI_FAILURE(acpi_get_handle(port, "UPSB.DSB0.NHI0", &nhi)))
+		return;
+
+	pci_info(dev, "mbp161 type3: NHI0.XRST(0) + NHI0.TRPE(1,0)\n");
+	acpi_execute_simple_method(nhi, "XRST", 0);
+	acpi_evaluate_object(nhi, "TRPE", &list, NULL);
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_RESUME_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x1905,
+			       quirk_mbp161_type3_resume);
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_RESUME_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x1909,
+			       quirk_mbp161_type3_resume);
 #endif
 
 /*
diff --git i/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c w/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
index bbd186c29ef7..7f230054da92 100644
--- i/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
+++ w/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/string_helpers.h>
 #include <linux/suspend.h>
+#include <linux/acpi.h>
+#include <linux/mbp161-tb.h>
 
 #include "nhi.h"
 #include "nhi_regs.h"
@@ -261,6 +263,108 @@ static const struct tb_nhi_ops pci_nhi_default_ops = {
 	.init_interrupts = nhi_pci_init_msi,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Apple Type3 (Titan Ridge) s2idle sequence.  VSEC+0x4c / +0x48 are PCI
+ * extended config (IOPCIDevice::extendedConfigWrite32/Read32).  Command 5 is
+ * (GO2SX=2 << 1) | VALID, the same encoding as icl_nhi_lc_mailbox_cmd.
+ * AppleThunderboltNHIType3::waitForOk2Go2Sx polls 30000 times with IODelay(10).
+ */
+#define APPLE_TR_TBT2PCIE	0x48
+#define APPLE_TR_PCIE2TBT	0x4c
+#define APPLE_TR_GO2SX_CMD	5
+#define APPLE_TR_GO2SX_DONE	4
+#define APPLE_TR_GO2SX_TRIES	0x7530
+
+static void apple_tr_nhi_acpi(struct tb_nhi *nhi, char *method, u64 arg)
+{
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI)
+	acpi_handle handle = ACPI_HANDLE(nhi->dev);
+
+	if (!handle)
+		return;
+	acpi_execute_simple_method(handle, method, arg);
+#endif
+}
+
+static int apple_tr_wait_go2sx(struct pci_dev *pdev, int vsec)
+{
+	u32 val = 0;
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < APPLE_TR_GO2SX_TRIES; i++) {
+		pci_read_config_dword(pdev, vsec + APPLE_TR_TBT2PCIE, &val);
+		if (val == 0xffffffff)
+			return -ENODEV;
+		if ((val & BIT(0)) && ((val & 0xfe) == APPLE_TR_GO2SX_DONE)) {
+			pci_write_config_dword(pdev, vsec + APPLE_TR_PCIE2TBT, 0);
+			return 0;
+		}
+		udelay(10);
+	}
+	return -ETIMEDOUT;
+}
+
+static int apple_tr_nhi_suspend_noirq(struct tb_nhi *nhi, bool wakeup)
+{
+	struct pci_dev *pdev = to_pci_dev(nhi->dev);
+	int vsec;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!mbp161_tb_type3_wanted())
+		return 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * Only the parts that need live config space belong here.  Cutting the
+	 * rail from this hook strands the NHI and every bridge above it: the
+	 * PCI core still has to walk them into D3hot afterwards, and they all
+	 * come back "Unable to change power state from D0 to D3hot".  SXFP(0)
+	 * and XRST(1) moved to quirk_mbp161_type3_suspend() on the root port.
+	 *
+	 * The Go2Sx mailbox is answered by the firmware connection manager.
+	 * Linux runs the software CM on Apple hardware (icm.c refuses
+	 * x86_apple_machine), and tb_switch_suspend() has already set
+	 * TB_LC_SX_CTRL_SLP on every link controller over the control channel,
+	 * which is the same notification by another route -- mainline skips
+	 * this mailbox for exactly that reason (see icl_nhi_suspend_noirq).
+	 * Send it anyway because Apple does, but a timeout here is expected
+	 * and is not a failure.
+	 */
+	vsec = pci_find_ext_capability(pdev, PCI_EXT_CAP_ID_VNDR);
+	if (!vsec) {
+		dev_err(nhi->dev, "mbp161 type3: no PCIe VSEC\n");
+	} else {
+		pci_write_config_dword(pdev, vsec + APPLE_TR_PCIE2TBT,
+				       APPLE_TR_GO2SX_CMD);
+		ret = apple_tr_wait_go2sx(pdev, vsec);
+		pci_info(pdev, "mbp161 type3: Go2Sx VSEC %#x ack %d%s\n",
+			 vsec, ret, ret ? " (expected under the software CM)" : "");
+	}
+
+	apple_tr_nhi_acpi(nhi, "RTPC", 0);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int apple_tr_nhi_resume_noirq(struct tb_nhi *nhi)
+{
+	if (!mbp161_tb_type3_wanted())
+		return 0;
+
+	apple_tr_nhi_acpi(nhi, "RTPC", 1);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct tb_nhi_ops apple_tr_nhi_ops = {
+	.pre_nvm_auth = nhi_pci_start_dma_port,
+	.post_nvm_auth = nhi_pci_complete_dma_port,
+	.request_ring_irq = nhi_pci_ring_request_msix,
+	.release_ring_irq = nhi_pci_ring_release_msix,
+	.shutdown = nhi_pci_shutdown,
+	.is_present = nhi_pci_is_present,
+	.init_interrupts = nhi_pci_init_msi,
+	.suspend_noirq = apple_tr_nhi_suspend_noirq,
+	.resume_noirq = apple_tr_nhi_resume_noirq,
+};
+
 /* Ice Lake specific NHI operations */
 
 #define ICL_LC_MAILBOX_TIMEOUT	500 /* ms */
@@ -532,8 +636,10 @@ static struct pci_device_id nhi_ids[] = {
 	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_ALPINE_RIDGE_C_2C_NHI) },
 	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_ALPINE_RIDGE_C_4C_NHI) },
 	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_ALPINE_RIDGE_C_USBONLY_NHI) },
-	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_2C_NHI) },
-	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_4C_NHI) },
+	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_2C_NHI),
+	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)&apple_tr_nhi_ops },
+	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_4C_NHI),
+	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)&apple_tr_nhi_ops },
 	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_ICL_NHI0),
 	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)&icl_nhi_ops },
 	{ PCI_VDEVICE(INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_ICL_NHI1),
diff --git i/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c w/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
index f43f2d952372..81d05e47aa06 100644
--- i/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
+++ w/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/errno.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/platform_data/x86/apple.h>
 
 #include "tb.h"
@@ -3148,13 +3149,19 @@ static int tb_resume_noirq(struct tb *tb)
 	tb_dbg(tb, "resuming...\n");
 
 	/*
-	 * For non-USB4 hosts (Apple systems) remove any PCIe devices
-	 * the firmware might have setup.
+	 * For non-USB4 hosts (Apple systems) remove any PCIe devices the
+	 * firmware might have setup. During suspend-to-idle the platform
+	 * firmware does not run and cannot have changed the topology.
 	 */
-	if (!tb_switch_is_usb4(tb->root_switch))
-		tb_switch_reset(tb->root_switch);
+	if (!tb_switch_is_usb4(tb->root_switch)) {
+		if (pm_suspend_no_platform())
+			tb_dbg(tb, "skipping host-router reset; platform firmware did not participate\n");
+		else
+			tb_switch_reset(tb->root_switch);
+	}
 
 	tb_switch_resume(tb->root_switch, false);
+
 	tb_free_invalid_tunnels(tb);
 	tb_free_unplugged_children(tb->root_switch);
 	tb_free_unplugged_xdomains(tb->root_switch);
@@ -3323,6 +3330,8 @@ static bool tb_apple_add_links(struct tb_nhi *nhi)
 	case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_CACTUS_RIDGE_4C:
 	case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_FALCON_RIDGE_2C_NHI:
 	case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_FALCON_RIDGE_4C_NHI:
+	case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_2C_NHI:
+	case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_4C_NHI:
 		break;
 	default:
 		return false;
diff --git i/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c w/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
index 6b3fcba44b08..87a5a7e4ff12 100644
--- i/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
+++ w/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/suspend.h>
+#include <linux/mbp161-tb.h>
 
 #include "xhci.h"
 #include "xhci-trace.h"
@@ -809,6 +810,24 @@ static void xhci_sparse_control_quirk(struct usb_hcd *hcd)
 	writel(reg, hcd->regs + SPARSE_CNTL_ENABLE);
 }
 
+static void xhci_pci_apple_rtpc(struct pci_dev *pdev, u64 enable)
+{
+	acpi_handle handle;
+
+	if (!mbp161_tb_type3_wanted())
+		return;
+	if (pdev->vendor != PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL ||
+	    pdev->device != PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_4C_XHCI)
+		return;
+
+	handle = ACPI_HANDLE(&pdev->dev);
+	if (!handle)
+		return;
+
+	pci_info(pdev, "mbp161 type3: xHCI RTPC(%llu)\n", enable);
+	acpi_execute_simple_method(handle, "RTPC", enable);
+}
+
 static int xhci_pci_suspend(struct usb_hcd *hcd, bool do_wakeup)
 {
 	struct xhci_hcd	*xhci = hcd_to_xhci(hcd);
@@ -846,6 +865,9 @@ static int xhci_pci_suspend(struct usb_hcd *hcd, bool do_wakeup)
 	if (ret && (xhci->quirks & XHCI_SSIC_PORT_UNUSED))
 		xhci_ssic_port_unused_quirk(hcd, false);
 
+	if (!ret)
+		xhci_pci_apple_rtpc(pdev, 0);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -855,6 +877,7 @@ static int xhci_pci_resume(struct usb_hcd *hcd, pm_message_t msg)
 	struct pci_dev *pdev = to_pci_dev(hcd->self.controller);
 	bool power_lost = msg.event == PM_EVENT_RESTORE;
 	bool is_auto_resume = msg.event == PM_EVENT_AUTO_RESUME;
+	int ret;
 
 	reset_control_reset(xhci->reset);
 
@@ -885,7 +908,10 @@ static int xhci_pci_resume(struct usb_hcd *hcd, pm_message_t msg)
 	if (xhci->quirks & XHCI_PME_STUCK_QUIRK)
 		xhci_pme_quirk(hcd);
 
-	return xhci_resume(xhci, power_lost, is_auto_resume);
+	ret = xhci_resume(xhci, power_lost, is_auto_resume);
+	if (!ret)
+		xhci_pci_apple_rtpc(pdev, 1);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int xhci_pci_poweroff_late(struct usb_hcd *hcd, bool do_wakeup)
diff --git i/include/linux/mbp161-tb.h w/include/linux/mbp161-tb.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..3442050e2135
--- /dev/null
+++ w/include/linux/mbp161-tb.h
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 */
+#ifndef _LINUX_MBP161_TB_H
+#define _LINUX_MBP161_TB_H
+
+#include <linux/types.h>
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI) && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PCI)
+bool mbp161_tb_type3_wanted(void);
+#else
+static inline bool mbp161_tb_type3_wanted(void)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif
